SurfaceBody: In the wooden chests just under the surface and in the chests of desert pyramids, from world creation
Pyramid: Pyramid treasure rooms
PyramidBody: Each desert pyramid hides one Gold Chest in its treasure room, from world creation
UndergroundBody: In every chest between the surface and the cavern layer, from world creation: Gold Chests of caves and cabins, biome chests, sky island and Dungeon chests
UndergroundGoldBody: In the Gold Chests of caves and cabins between the surface and the cavern layer, from world creation
Cavern: Cavern chests
CavernBody: In every chest from the cavern layer down to the Underworld, from world creation: Gold Chests of caves and cabins, biome chests, temple and Dungeon chests
CavernGoldBody: In the Gold Chests of caves and cabins from the cavern layer down to the Underworld, from world creation
Deep: Underworld chests
DeepBody: In the Shadow Chests of the Underworld and the few Gold Chests just above it, from world creation
DeepGoldBody: In the few Gold Chests just above the Underworld, from world creation
Shadow: Shadow Chests in the Underworld
ShadowBody: In the ruined houses of the Underworld, locked since the world was made: a {1} opens them
IceBody: In the Frozen Chests of the underground ice biome and its cabins, from world creation
DesertBody: In the Sandstone Chests of the underground desert and its houses, from world creation
JungleShrine: Jungle shrines
JungleShrineBody: In the Ivy Chest of each jungle shrine, from world creation
Mahogany: Living mahogany trees
MahoganyBody: In the Ivy Chest inside each living mahogany tree of the underground jungle, from world creation
WaterBody: In the Water Chests that lie under water across the world, from world creation
OceanCave: Ocean cave
OceanCaveBody: Some worlds have a cave by the ocean with one Water Chest, from world creation
SkyBody: In the Skyware Chest of each sky island house, from world creation
Temple: Lihzahrd Chests
TempleBody: In the chests of the Jungle Temple, from world creation; its door opens with the {1}, which {0} drops
DungeonGoldBody: In the Dungeon's rooms, locked since the world was made: a {1} opens them, and the Dungeon lets you in once {0} is defeated
DungeonWoodenBody: In the wooden chests of the Dungeon's rooms, from world creation; the Dungeon lets you in once {0} is defeated
BiomeChests: Dungeon: Biome Chests
BiomeChestsBody: The Dungeon's Biome Chests, locked since the world was made: each opens with its own key, and only once {0} is defeated
DrunkBody: In a drunk world (seed 05162020), in any chest that holds something, when the world is made
Workshop: Rusted workshops
WorkshopBody: Draedon's small workshops in the deep caverns, several per world with one chest each, from world creation
Outpost: Research outposts
OutpostBody: Draedon's research outposts in the deep caverns, a few per world with one chest each, from world creation
HellLabBody: Draedon's laboratory in the Underworld has two chests, from world creation
SunkenLab: Draedon's lab by the Sunken Sea
IceLab: Draedon's lab in the ice biome
PlagueLab: Draedon's lab in the jungle
PlanetoidLab: Draedon's lab in the sky
CavernLab: Draedon's lab in the caverns
LabBody: One laboratory per world with two chests, from world creation
CorruptionShrine: Corruption shrine
CrimsonShrine: Crimson shrine
DesertShrine: Desert shrine
GraniteShrine: Granite shrine
IceShrine: Ice shrine
MarbleShrine: Marble shrine
MushroomShrine: Mushroom shrine
SurfaceShrine: Surface shrine
AbyssShrine: Abyss shrine
ShimmerShrine: Shimmer shrine
ShrineBody: A hidden shrine with one chest, one per world, from world creation
AbyssShrineBody: A Void Chest at the bottom of the Abyss, one per world, from world creation
AbyssChestsBody: In the locked chests on the islands of the Abyss, from world creation; they open once {0} is defeated
Sulphur: Rusty chests of the Sulphurous Sea
SulphurBody: Four Rusty Chests by and under the Sulphurous Sea, from world creation
Crag: Brimstone Crag bridge
CragBody: Two Ashen Chests on the bridge over the Brimstone Crag, from world creation
Honey: Honey chests
HoneyBody: In the Honey Chests of the Giant Hive in the underground jungle and of the mud planetoids in the sky, from world creation
MudPlanet: Mud planetoids
MudPlanetBody: Some mud planetoids in the sky hold a Water Chest, from world creation
Vernal: Vernal Pass
VernalBody: Five Ivy Chests in the Vernal Pass by the Jungle Temple, from world creation
MechanicShed: Mechanic's shed
MechanicShedBody: A shed on the surface of the snow biome with one chest, from world creation
Archive: Forsaken Archive
ArchiveBody: Two chests in a hidden library of the Dungeon, from world creation; the Dungeon lets you in once {0} is defeated
EvilIsland: Sky island of the other evil
EvilIslandBody: A sky island of the evil your world lacks, with one chest, from world creation
SkyHouses: The first {0} sky island houses each hold a different one of these, any further house one of them at random
InPlaceOfEye: Calamity puts it in place of the {0} in wooden, rich mahogany, ivy, ice, Lihzahrd, granite, marble, sandstone and trapped chests
EyeKept: With Calamity only water, web-covered and Biome Chests keep it; the others get other loot in its place
PerChest: Chance and amount per chest
WorldOre: Only in a world with this ore: each world has one ore of each pair
OneChest: Only one of its chests holds it
OtherChests: Each of its other chests holds one of these
AboveCaverns: Only in those above the cavern layer
InCaverns: Only in those in the cavern layer
BelowLava: Only in those below the lava line
GoldOnly: Only in their Gold Chests, the Dungeon's locked ones too
WholeSet: The whole set comes together
InTurn: The chests take these in turn, so a world with few of them can lack one
UpperDesert: Only in the upper part of the underground desert
LowerDesert: Only in its deeper part
ClickChestCard: Click: the {0}'s card
SummonedWith: Summoned with {0}
FromBossChecklist: From Boss Checklist
FromBossRegistration: From the mod's entry for Boss Checklist
WhereSummoned: Wherever it is summoned
DuringFight: During {0}'s fight
WhereItsBossFights: Wherever {0} is fought
During: During {0}
CultistRitual: Outside the Dungeon, while the cultists hold their ritual
MovesIn: Moves into a free house
AnyTime: Any time
WhereTheEventIs: Wherever the event is
FromBossCode: From the boss's own code
FromGameCode: From the game's code
